{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jAupzgZN4iREnKqWnGZm5","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/docs/specs/WI-274.md b/docs/specs/WI-274.md\nindex ac6568d..d594bce 100644\n--- a/docs/specs/WI-274.md\n+++ b/docs/specs/WI-274.md\n@@ -125,9 +125,12 @@ Design calls left to the build session (recorded in IF-068's notes):\n   `[agent-loop]` block (now framed as the opt-in single home) plus a pointer\n   comment by the `AGENT_JOBS` slot in `agent-resume.template.{sh,cmd}` both name\n   the opt-in home and the precedence — a downstream repo moves to it exactly as\n-  this meta-repo's own launchers did (uncomment `[agent-loop]`, blank the launcher\n-  slots). `agent-resume.template.command` is a pure delegator with no dial slots,\n-  so it needs no change.\n+  this meta-repo's own launchers did (uncomment `[agent-loop]`, keep the model\n+  slots blank, then make the stated exact jobs edit: POSIX replaces the default\n+  line with `unset AGENT_JOBS` and removes it from the export list; Windows\n+  replaces the conditional default with `set \"AGENT_JOBS=\"`, which deletes the\n+  variable). `agent-resume.template.command` is a pure delegator with no dial\n+  slots, so it needs no change.\n \n **Trade-off accepted:** a double-clicking user no longer sees the dials in the\n file they clicked — mitigated by the launcher comment naming the declared home.\ndiff --git a/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.cmd b/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.cmd\nindex 2850775..55d4030 100644\n--- a/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.cmd\n+++ b/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.cmd\n@@ -50,9 +50,11 @@ REM An inherited AGENT_JOBS wins over this default; an absent/empty value\n REM still boots the dispatcher at its own default (the legacy serial resume\n REM driver is retired).\n REM Single-home option (IF-068): to avoid editing jobs/model/model-map in each\n-REM of the three launchers, declare them once in docs\\stack.ini [agent-loop] and\n-REM blank these slots - agent_loop resolves CLI flag ^> AGENT_* env ^> that file\n-REM ^> default. Opt-in: a fresh scaffold keeps the dials in the launcher.\n+REM of the three launchers, declare them once in docs\\stack.ini [agent-loop].\n+REM Keep AGENT_MODEL / AGENT_MODEL_MAP blank; for jobs, replace the next line\n+REM with `set \"AGENT_JOBS=\"` (CMD deletes the variable). This exact Windows edit\n+REM leaves no launcher env override, so agent_loop resolves CLI flag ^> AGENT_*\n+REM env ^> that file ^> default. Opt-in: a fresh scaffold keeps its dials here.\n if not defined AGENT_JOBS set \"AGENT_JOBS=2\"\n REM Per-session wall-clock bound (seconds) so one hung CLI cannot wedge a\n REM lane forever - the walk-away guarantee. Blank the slot to disable\ndiff --git a/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.sh b/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.sh\nindex f4639db..8992ba2 100644\n--- a/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.sh\n+++ b/project-trajectory/scripts/agent-resume.template.sh\n@@ -49,9 +49,12 @@ AGENT_CMD_INTERACTIVE=\"\"\n # boots the dispatcher at its own default (the legacy serial resume driver is\n # retired).\n # Single-home option (IF-068): to avoid editing jobs/model/model-map in each of\n-# the three launchers, declare them once in docs/stack.ini [agent-loop] and blank\n-# these slots — agent_loop resolves CLI flag > AGENT_* env > that file > default.\n-# Opt-in: a fresh scaffold keeps the dials in the launcher by default.\n+# the three launchers, declare them once in docs/stack.ini [agent-loop]. Keep\n+# AGENT_MODEL / AGENT_MODEL_MAP blank; for jobs, replace the next line with\n+# `unset AGENT_JOBS` AND remove AGENT_JOBS from the export line below. That exact\n+# POSIX edit leaves no launcher env override, so agent_loop resolves CLI flag >\n+# AGENT_* env > that file > default. Opt-in: a fresh scaffold keeps its dials in\n+# the launcher by default.\n AGENT_JOBS=\"${AGENT_JOBS:-2}\"\n # Per-session wall-clock bound (seconds) so one hung CLI cannot wedge a lane\n # forever — the walk-away guarantee. Blank to disable (engine default 0 = no\ndiff --git a/project-trajectory/stack.ini.template b/project-trajectory/stack.ini.template\nindex 98d0b57..170e683 100644\n--- a/project-trajectory/stack.ini.template\n+++ b/project-trajectory/stack.ini.template\n@@ -102,13 +102,21 @@ docs/status.md = status | <!-- BEGIN GENERATED STATUS --> | <!-- END GENERATED S\n # falls through — so this section is OPTIONAL and ships COMMENTED OUT: by default a\n # fresh scaffold keeps its dials in the launchers (agent-resume.*, where a\n # double-clicking user sees them next to the consent banner), and an absent\n-# [agent-loop] behaves exactly as before. Uncomment this section AND blank the\n-# matching launcher slots to move to the single home — the migration the kit's own\n-# meta-repo took for its frequently-turned dials; a fresh adopter usually needn't:\n+# [agent-loop] behaves exactly as before. To opt in, uncomment this section,\n+# leave AGENT_MODEL / AGENT_MODEL_MAP blank, and make the exact jobs edit beside\n+# the launcher slots: POSIX replaces `AGENT_JOBS=\"${AGENT_JOBS:-2}\"` with\n+# `unset AGENT_JOBS` and removes it from the export line; Windows replaces\n+# `if not defined AGENT_JOBS set \"AGENT_JOBS=2\"` with `set \"AGENT_JOBS=\"`.\n+# Those edits leave AGENT_JOBS absent, so this file wins. That is the migration\n+# the kit's own meta-repo took for its frequently-turned dials; a fresh adopter\n+# usually needn't:\n # [agent-loop]\n-# jobs = 2                 # dispatcher worker ceiling (int, 1 = serial, or auto)\n-# model = <strong-model>   # fallback {model} when managed routing is off (AGENT_MODEL)\n-# model-map = PLAN=<strong-model>,BUILD=<cheap-model>   # per-phase fallback (AGENT_MODEL_MAP)\n+# jobs = 2\n+# dispatcher worker ceiling: an int (1 = serial) or auto.\n+# model = <strong-model>\n+# fallback {model} when managed routing is off (AGENT_MODEL).\n+# model-map = PLAN=<strong-model>,BUILD=<cheap-model>\n+# per-phase fallback (AGENT_MODEL_MAP).\n \n # --- Run capabilities (the launcher menu) ------------------------------------\n # The root run.cmd / run.sh / run.command launchers read this [run] section\ndiff --git a/tests/test_bootstrap.py b/tests/test_bootstrap.py\nindex 361faf6..566842e 100644\n--- a/tests/test_bootstrap.py\n+++ b/tests/test_bootstrap.py\n@@ -457,6 +457,51 @@ def test_default_scaffold_leaves_agent_resume_unseeded(scaffold):\n     assert 'AGENT_CMD=\"\"' in sh\n \n \n+def test_scaffolded_launcher_single_home_migration_lets_config_jobs_win(\n+    scaffold, monkeypatch\n+):\n+    # WI-274 / IF-068: the opt-in instructions must mechanically remove the\n+    # template's fresh-scaffold jobs=2 default. Merely \"blanking\" that slot used\n+    # to re-apply 2 through `${AGENT_JOBS:-2}`, silently beating [agent-loop].\n+    sh_path = scaffold / \"agent-resume.sh\"\n+    cmd_path = scaffold / \"agent-resume.cmd\"\n+    sh = sh_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+    cmd = cmd_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+\n+    # Apply the exact documented migration to the real scaffolded launchers.\n+    # POSIX must both clear an inherited value and stop re-exporting it; CMD's\n+    # `set \"NAME=\"` deletes the inherited variable in that process.\n+    migrated_sh = sh.replace(\n+        'AGENT_JOBS=\"${AGENT_JOBS:-2}\"', \"unset AGENT_JOBS\"\n+    ).replace(\" AGENT_JOBS\\nPY=\", \"\\nPY=\")\n+    migrated_cmd = cmd.replace(\n+        'if not defined AGENT_JOBS set \"AGENT_JOBS=2\"', 'set \"AGENT_JOBS=\"'\n+    )\n+    assert \"unset AGENT_JOBS\" in migrated_sh\n+    assert 'AGENT_JOBS=\"${AGENT_JOBS:-2}\"' not in migrated_sh\n+    assert \"export AGENT_CMD\" in migrated_sh and \"AGENT_JOBS\\nPY=\" not in migrated_sh\n+    assert 'set \"AGENT_JOBS=\"' in migrated_cmd\n+    assert 'if not defined AGENT_JOBS set \"AGENT_JOBS=2\"' not in migrated_cmd\n+\n+    # Materialize the commented s